The code runs over trees provided by Jaebeom for both OO data and MC

1. getDijets.C makes histograms of reconstructed xj and reconstructed pt1pt2. For MC this also produces the response matrices
***projectDijets.C (reads in output from getDijets.C) takes these histograms and does the xj projection
***draw_hists.C (reads in output from getDijets.C and projectDijets.C) draws the histograms for reco xj, the projection closure test, and reco dphi distributions

2. unfoldClosure.C (reads in output from getDijets.C) runs the unfolding on the reco MC
***projectUnfoldClosure.C (reads in output from unfoldClosure.C) does the xj projection on the unfolded/truth/measured hists
***drawunfoldclosure.C (reads in output from projectUnfoldClosure.C) draws the closure test histograms
Both projectUnfoldClosure() and drawunfoldclosure() have the option to do the half or full closure. It defaults to running the half closure test.